WEBVTT

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.510
Ren, are you awake?

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:08.110
Yeah.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:10.610
You slept well.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.740
You hardly ate anything yesterday.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:14.940
You must be hungry.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.620
No, not really.

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:21.620
<i>His eyes are swollen from crying.</i>

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:26.020
You're going to Kiri-chan's place 
today to train Lyuba, right?

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:26.810
What time?

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.000
Ten. I can go out?

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:34.790
Sure. It's something you had already 
scheduled with Kiri-chan.

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:36.760
Go on, take a bath and get ready.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:40.890
<i>I never imagined that Ren...</i>

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:49.620
<i>would ever cry like that, but...</i>

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:22.740
Ren? Ren!

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:25.490
What?

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:29.600
You don't seem well. 
Should we call it quits for today?

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:31.120
I'm fine.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.120
I appreciate the help, though.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:37.510
No one in my family 
knows how to handle dogs.

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:42.140
Ren-kun, Kiri, lunch is ready.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:43.870
You'll stay for lunch, right?

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.140
Actually, I...

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:49.490
I heard Kiri had dinner at 
your place the other day.

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:52.690
Since I heard you were coming over 
today, I put in some extra effort.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.620
You heard her. 
Do you need to call Haru-san?

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:06.960
<i>I don't know anything 
about phones these days.</i>

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:09.430
<i>Maybe I should've brought Aki or Shima.</i>

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:11.420
What kind of phone are you looking for?

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:15.860
These types of phones with a focus on 
features are popular among young men.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:16.800
Excuse me.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:19.380
<i>Haru.</i>

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:23.060
Ren? Sorry, I'm out of the house right now.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:24.150
If it's about lunch...

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:26.530
<i>Kiri's family made lunch for me.</i>

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:29.350
That's good. Make sure to thank them.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:30.680
<i>Okay.</i>

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:34.950
<i>By the way, I was just 
looking at some new phones.</i>

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:36.480
<i>What kind do you want?</i>

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:40.690
Gramps isn't paying me until 
after I finish the whole job.

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:42.200
<i>I know.</i>

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:44.950
But it's inconvenient for me 
if you don't have one.

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:48.010
<i>You can pay me back.</i>

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:51.610
Fine. I'll leave it up to you, then.

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:52.370
<i>Got it.</i>

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:59.960
<i>I felt like something had 
changed a little recently...</i>

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:04.190
<i>But Haru's back to being 
my older brother again.</i>

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:07.470
<i>I messed up yesterday.</i>

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:11.770
I never taught you to do 
this in front of people.

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:15.730
<i>He probably thought I was too immature.</i>

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:18.270
<i>I shouldn't have done that.</i>

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:20.200
What did Haru-san say?

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:24.990
He was out of the house 
and hadn't made lunch yet.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:26.000
Great.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.530
He told me to thank your parents.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:31.720
Oh, please. We should be thanking you.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:33.790
Chew Chew

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:33.790
Lyuba's such a rascal.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:41.300
Chew

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.520
His boss forced him to take Lyuba

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:38.890
after he learned it was his 
dream to own a large dog.

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:41.300
He probably couldn't handle Lyuba, either.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:46.410
I see. You're lucky you 
came to this home, Lyuba.

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:52.280
Why is he so well-mannered around Ren-kun?

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:54.310
Dogs watch their humans closely.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.800
As head of the household, 
you should act more important.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:00.820
Kiri, why are you laughing?

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:05.820
By the way, Ren-kun, 
what's your brother's café like?

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.610
I'd like to check it out, but isn't it busy?

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:13.110
It should be fine if you come right 
at opening time on a weekday.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:15.790
Oh, that won't work. It's summer vacation.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:16.930
Really?

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:20.510
Lots of young women who normally 
can't come during the week

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:22.740
hang around there before they open.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:25.500
And they're all there to see 
your brother, of course.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:27.090
I didn't know.

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:30.060
He cooks for his family and runs the store.

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:32.720
There's no man like him, for sure.

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:34.190
<i>She's right.</i>

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:39.230
Men like Haru-chan tend to end up 
with high-maintenance women, too.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:39.230
High-maintenance

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:43.740
The other day, Otomo-san gave 
Haru-chan a marriage meeting photo.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:44.990
What?!

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:47.990
Bro, did you get a new phone?

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:49.720
It's for Ren.

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:53.990
Making decisions without his input again?
He's going to be pissed again.

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:56.440
I'm making him pay me back.

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.680
And he needs to have one 
on him if he's going out.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:02.270
Oh, really? Just how 
overprotective are you?

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:04.000
What? Aki, are you going out?

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.010
To work. I don't need dinner.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:11.540
Since Aki won't be here, 
I'll make fish for dinner.

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:15.290
Whoops. Hello?

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:17.170
<i>Huh? Who is this?</i>

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:19.280
<i>Isn't this Ren's phone?</i>

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:23.120
Yes, it is. I'm Ren's brother.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:24.280
Who are you?

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:29.030
Damn it, he hung up! Who was that?

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:33.580
That was close. Was that Haru?

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:40.590
<i>Hello? It's Ren.</i>

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:43.050
Man, don't scare me like that.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.740
Haru answered your cell phone 
when I called it just now.

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:48.050
<i>More importantly, why did 
you give me that money?</i>

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:49.610
<i>Because of you—</i>

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:52.750
Did Haru find out about the money?

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:54.570
<i>I said I didn't need it.</i>

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:57.680
Weren't you trying to make some money?

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:01.150
Haru said it's more than 
I should be making in one night.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.190
In any case, I'm returning it.

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:05.340
Come get it now.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:09.060
<i>What? But I just got home from work.</i>

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:10.950
<i>You're not going to come here?</i>

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.520
<i>Don't be ridiculous!</i>

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:15.610
<i>If you won't come, 
I'm telling Haru all about you!</i>

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:17.450
Fine, fine!

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:20.410
I guess I don't have a choice.

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:24.060
Hey.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:27.840
You're late.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.360
It took me a while to find a place to park.

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:32.550
I got here as quickly as I could.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:36.290
Anyway, why don't we go inside
somewhere? It's hot out here.

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:37.810
I'm thirsty.

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:40.100
This won't take long.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:41.740
Here's your money.

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:44.790
You can stop somewhere on your way home.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.310
You really are unlovable...

00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:49.800
Later. I'm going home.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:52.010
Wait, Ren! Hey!

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:54.530
Did Haru find the money and get mad at you?

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:56.720
Did you tell him about me?

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.040
Glare

00:07:58.790 --> 00:07:59.560
Ow!

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:01.790
That hurt...

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:05.470
Hey, wait! I'm sorry, okay?

00:08:05.470 --> 00:08:07.170
I'm sorry, Ren!

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:10.850
Let go! I don't want 
anything else to do with you!

00:08:11.230 --> 00:08:15.430
I don't like keeping secrets from Haru, 
and nothing good comes of being around you!

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:17.380
Nothing good?

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:19.480
Did Haru hit you or something?

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:23.020
Haru would never hit me, but...

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.060
But?

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:33.020
Aw, jeez! What's wrong with you?

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:35.070
Huh?

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:38.370
Is that Ren Ren and Haru-san?

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:37.820
There, there.

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:39.280
Don't touch me!

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:40.470
No, that's not him.

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:41.080
Good boy. Look this way.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:44.370
Several 
Days 
Later

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:43.420
I'm going out.

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:44.580
Be careful.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:46.080
Haru-san.

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:48.930
Is Ren Ren going to clean again?

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:50.840
Yeah, apparently.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:52.590
Haru-san, what are you looking—

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:55.020
A GPS?!

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:56.780
Modern phones sure are convenient.

00:08:57.190 --> 00:08:59.900
I know exactly where he is 
if he has his phone on him.

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:01.600
That sounds criminal!

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:05.600
I'm his guardian. 
You got a problem with that?

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:09.980
No, but does Ren Ren know about that?

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:11.280
I'll tell him if he asks.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:12.860
Jeez, sounds like a scam.

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:16.880
Say whatever you want. 
He's been acting weird lately.

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:19.550
After staying out all night, he brought 
home an unnatural amount of money,

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:21.750
and some strange man called his phone.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:23.870
Speaking of strange men...

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:26.870
That wasn't you this past Sunday, was it?

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:30.470
It looked like you from behind, 
but the situation seemed strange.

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:35.380
<i>Strange men and strange situations?</i>

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:40.500
Ren, have you gotten used to your new phone?

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:43.660
I haven't really used it yet, so I'm not sure.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:47.250
I'd like it if you'd e-mail 
or call me sometimes.

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:52.090
We live together. Why do I need to do that?

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:54.150
I'll call you if I need something.

00:09:54.930 --> 00:10:01.160
Then what did the man you met 
the other day want with you?

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:03.200
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:07.800
That's pretty bold for such a terrible liar!

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:10.230
Did that man give you the money, too?

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:11.670
I returned the money.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:14.250
I haven't done anything wrong,

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:16.080
and I don't have anything else to say.

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:17.420
It's none of your business!

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:23.430
<i>Sometimes I think he's a genius 
at pushing all my buttons.</i>

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:26.930
Haru?

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:31.290
I'm in the mood. 
Entertain me for a little while.

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:32.940
Wh-Where did this come from?

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:36.940
You're a man, too. 
You understand what it's like.

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:45.130
<i>What I really want to do is pretend I have 
no idea what's going on and gently hold him.</i>

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:46.510
Haru...

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:01.720
<i>Nothing ever goes right.</i>

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:04.160
Oh, damn it!

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:04.960
Haru?

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:06.570
Ren, give me your phone!

00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:08.010
Wh-Why all of a sudden?

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:09.140
Just give it to me.

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:13.230
Who are you calling in 
the middle of the night?

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:15.810
Ren, you just be quiet.

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:16.440
Ha—

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:18.690
<i>What is it, Ren?</i>

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:21.740
<i>Sorry, I'm at work right now. 
I'll call you back—</i>

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:24.950
You work pretty late hours.

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:26.800
Who are you, anyway?

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:30.250
If you mess with Ren again, I'll kill you.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:33.410
What? What's wrong?

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:32.660
<i>Haru!</i>

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:34.370
<i>I told you to be quiet!</i>

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:38.510
You really don't know who I am, Haru?

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:39.280
Sheesh.

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:42.220
I guess it can't be helped. 
It's been ten years.

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:45.970
We might not recognize each other 
if we ran into each other around town.

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:47.970
Huh? Ten years?

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:51.370
<i>What time do you finish work tomorrow?</i>

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:53.070
Huh? Six.

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:55.180
<i>I'll head to your place around then.</i>

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:57.270
<i>Don't be too mean to your youngest brother.</i>

00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:58.080
<i>Bye.</i>

00:11:58.080 --> 00:11:58.720
Huh?

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:03.740
Huh? Do I... know him?

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:04.830
Re—

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:05.800
That's not my problem!

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:07.740
Huh?

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:09.990
Wait, Ren!

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:13.500
Hey, it's been a while.

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:19.860
That face! You're Natsuo!

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:21.510
Does that make you Aki?

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:23.230
Whoa, what the heck?

00:12:23.230 --> 00:12:25.530
You're twins, but you look nothing alike.

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:26.510
Shut up!

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:28.530
What? Are you really Natsuo?

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:32.630
Haru, because you used a misleading 
name while working in Kabukicho,

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:34.360
I've had to deal with a lot of crap.

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:38.070
What? Are you the host 
they call the Second Haru?

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:39.780
Yeah, sorry about that!

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:43.860
Natsuo, you bastard! 
How dare you come back to Japan?!

00:12:42.580 --> 00:12:43.860
Now, now.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:47.280
His dad's debts caused our 
family a lot of trouble, too!

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:51.280
Because they ran from their debts, 
our parents had to work like crazy!

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:53.250
Sorry about that.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:55.790
Huh? I thought you were living 
in Hawaii with your dad.

00:12:56.670 --> 00:13:00.780
I was, until this spring. My dad remarried.

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:04.480
I thought I'd try working 
in Japan for a little bit,

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:07.550
and now everyone's mistaking 
me for you in Kabukicho.

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:11.430
I heard you'd gotten a fourth 
brother at some point

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:13.500
and even opened a café.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:15.060
I'm your cousin. Of course I was curious.

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:18.020
It was a coincidence that I found 
the youngest brother, though.

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:20.320
It's amusing how serious he is.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:25.410
When I told him to keep me a secret 
from you, he kept his promise.

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:34.370
Ren, I'll hire professionals to 
handle the rest. You can stop.

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:37.540
I'll wipe the windows and 
finish cleaning the yard.

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:40.710
You'll do all of that, too? Thanks.

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:44.030
I'll leave the apartment keys here.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:45.950
Don't forget to lock the windows.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:46.820
Got it.

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:52.080
<i>I only lived in this building 
with Haru for six months,</i>

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:54.760
<i>but I feel nostalgic being here.</i>

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:57.700
I'm going to get Ren.

00:13:59.710 --> 00:14:00.810
Ow...

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:06.820
Haru actually hit me. 
Who hits a host in the face?

00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:09.840
You knew he would hit you, didn't you?

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:12.830
You wanted to make him mad.

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:17.610
You haven't changed much, Natsuo.

00:14:18.140 --> 00:14:19.380
<i>That's right.</i>

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:24.840
<i>I hated the way Haru always 
acted like such a good boy.</i>

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:39.720
Hey.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:43.010
Did you have business in that room?

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:46.690
Ikuyoshi, the man who lives there, 
should be coming home soon.

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:47.470
You can wait for him.

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:50.390
N-No, I'm in a hurry. 
I'll come back another time.

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:51.180
Hey.

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:52.060
Ren.

00:14:52.630 --> 00:14:55.080
What are you doing up there?

00:14:55.430 --> 00:14:59.180
You hadn't come back yet, 
so Gramps was worried about you.

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:01.880
Get out of the way!

00:15:03.430 --> 00:15:04.130
Ren!

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:19.230
Ow...

00:15:19.570 --> 00:15:20.960
Are you okay, Ren?

00:15:21.470 --> 00:15:22.020
Haru!

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:22.940
Haru!

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:24.020
Haru!

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:26.650
Kaidou Ren

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:26.650
Here's your pay.

00:15:27.270 --> 00:15:29.640
Thanks, Gramps. Here, Haru.

00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:30.570
Huh?

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:33.660
At least count it, you little brat.

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:35.270
He's right, Ren.

00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:37.470
Don't give it to me without 
even checking what's inside.

00:15:37.470 --> 00:15:38.580
It's for the phone.

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:45.790
Wait, what? Isn't this a bit 
much for the job Ren did?

00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:49.530
It was cheaper than hiring professionals.

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:52.010
On top of that, Ren did a great job.

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:54.800
That's right. The police sang his praises, too.

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:59.060
Was he the former resident 
of that garbage room?

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:02.670
Yeah. Apparently, he'd been coming 
from time to time to check on his room

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:06.570
and breaking into the other 
apartments to look for valuables.

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:09.700
And Ren caught him in the act.

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:12.330
Breaking open those weak locks is too easy.

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:15.070
Shut up! I switched them 
all out for new ones!

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:18.830
I'm really grateful to Ren Ren, though.

00:16:19.190 --> 00:16:22.980
He saved my expensive watch 
and premium sneakers.

00:16:23.440 --> 00:16:25.830
Those all came from me.

00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:28.830
If you ask me, it wasn't a good thing.

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:31.840
Haru got hurt because of me.

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:35.840
Don't worry about it. 
It's just a little fracture.

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:39.370
So minus what you owe me for the phone,

00:16:39.370 --> 00:16:42.350
you can spend the rest of your 
earnings however you want.

00:16:43.410 --> 00:16:44.450
I know.

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:51.030
Haru, do you want some coffee?

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:54.280
I'll do the shopping, 
and I'll clean the house, too.

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:59.240
Tanuki, Haru's hurt. Stay away from him.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:01.250
What? Really?

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:06.590
You know, Ren, I did take the day 
off work because of my injury,

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:10.320
but I'm not so badly hurt that you 
need to keep me away from everything.

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:12.620
Besides, I have absolutely nothing to do.

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:13.810
It's fine once in a while.

00:17:14.490 --> 00:17:17.650
Ikuyoshi said you work too much.

00:17:18.090 --> 00:17:19.540
I agree.

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:20.510
Yeah, yeah.

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:24.580
Also, I'm going to help around 
Mikiko's office starting tomorrow.

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:27.020
What? You got another job?

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:31.000
But you had money leftover after paying 
for the phone from working for the old man.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:32.890
You can never have too much money.

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.530
And I can't refuse a request from Mikiko.

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:39.640
Come here, Ren.

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:40.530
What?

00:17:41.130 --> 00:17:44.990
You haven't been sleeping 
in my room lately. Why not?

00:17:44.990 --> 00:17:47.640
I'm not sleeping with you until your arm heals.

00:17:48.060 --> 00:17:49.290
It still hurts, doesn't it?

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:53.750
I'm fine. It's worse for me
when you're not around.

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:55.990
Then I'll stay with you until you fall asleep.

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:57.800
How's that?

00:17:58.290 --> 00:18:00.790
<i>Why is he being so stubborn?</i>

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:01.260
Hmph

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:04.310
<i>Things haven't been going 
right for a while now.</i>

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:08.690
Ren, do you not want to kiss me?

00:18:09.070 --> 00:18:09.940
I do.

00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:12.060
Then kiss me.

00:18:15.770 --> 00:18:17.430
Your mouth...

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:18.940
H-Haru!

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:19.970
What?

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:22.330
Don't! Don't touch me!

00:18:22.720 --> 00:18:25.500
What? Because I'm injured?

00:18:28.450 --> 00:18:31.430
<i>Seriously? I'm going to die of frustration!</i>

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:36.310
But I'll kiss you.

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:48.480
<i>Damn it... How can he be so cute?</i>

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:50.730
Damn it, I can't hold back anymore!

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:53.320
What are you to me, anyway?

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:54.600
I don't know—

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:01.890
There's something wrong with me.

00:19:02.430 --> 00:19:06.750
I love you. I want to be 
nice to you and cherish you.

00:19:07.150 --> 00:19:09.940
But remember how you cried 
in front of me the other day?

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:13.750
I wasn't crying. I won't cry anymore.

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:18.180
Yeah, I know. That was crazy.

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:20.510
It was such a rush.

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:25.010
Just imagining your crying face turns me on.

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:29.850
In fact, it makes me want 
to make you cry even more.

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:30.160
Sadist

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:32.520
Sadist

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:33.020
<i>A switch inside him just flipped!</i>

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:38.290
<i>But I'm starving, too.</i>

00:19:39.310 --> 00:19:41.380
<i>I want this man to be mine.</i>

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:44.450
<i>Nothing I've said until now has worked.</i>

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:47.000
Haru...

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:52.200
<i>Against such a beautiful, 
kind, and unfair man,</i>

00:19:52.760 --> 00:19:55.040
<i>I didn't stand a chance.</i>

00:19:55.760 --> 00:19:59.910
<i>If it will make him mine, 
if that's his weakness,</i>

00:20:00.310 --> 00:20:02.050
<i>then I'll use it against him.</i>

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:03.800
We're home.

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:07.930
Jeez, who's going to cook 
dinner when our bro's hurt?

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.810
Shopping is such a pain in the ass.

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:13.030
Now, now. We bought beef today.

00:20:13.030 --> 00:20:14.880
Steaks, steaks!

00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:16.880
Aki, you should eat your vegetables, too.

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:17.940
Hey!

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:21.890
Don't leave me behind like that.

00:20:21.890 --> 00:20:23.570
What am I supposed to do with this dog food?

00:20:25.110 --> 00:20:26.270
Ask Ren.

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:28.310
What? Where is he?

00:20:28.310 --> 00:20:31.330
He's flirting with our idiot 
brother on the couch over there.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.780
What are you guys doing 
on that cramped couch?!

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:37.800
Gross!

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:40.570
That bastard...

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:41.590
I'll kill him.

00:20:42.370 --> 00:20:45.590
<i>Someone's always getting in the way 
just when things are getting good.</i>

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:48.720
What's wrong with this dog? 
Is this even a dog?

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:50.850
Don't you think it's too round?

00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:53.600
Natsuo, go home already!

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:54.990
All the way back to Hawaii!

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:57.730
<i>And so his punishment ended.</i>

00:22:32.070 --> 00:22:34.520
I drank too much.

00:22:34.520 --> 00:22:36.410
Why did you stay here?

00:22:39.940 --> 00:22:41.590
What? No way!

00:22:41.590 --> 00:22:45.160
The Natsu of Kabukicho that everyone's 
been talking about was Haru's cousin?

00:22:45.160 --> 00:22:46.300
They look exactly alike.

00:22:46.500 --> 00:22:50.880
You think so? Natsuo's the gaudy one, 
and our bro's the useless one.

00:22:50.880 --> 00:22:52.300
Oh, right.

00:22:52.850 --> 00:22:56.440
I bet you mistake them 
for each other sometimes.

00:22:57.780 --> 00:23:00.560
Never. I can tell them apart by their smell.

00:23:01.110 --> 00:23:02.400
Their smell?

00:23:02.740 --> 00:23:03.570
Ren!

00:23:04.190 --> 00:23:05.190
Really?

00:23:05.770 --> 00:23:07.600
That's convenient, then.

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:11.320
I noticed while doing the laundry

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:15.080
that our bro and Natsuo wear the 
same brand and size of underwear.

00:23:15.740 --> 00:23:16.580
Now, then...

00:23:17.090 --> 00:23:18.750
Which one is our brother's?

00:23:21.910 --> 00:23:25.150
We had Tanuki determine whose was whose.

00:23:25.590 --> 00:23:26.510
This one!

00:23:26.970 --> 00:23:29.440
Really? Good boy, Tanuki.

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:40.380
Next Time
